From 4de8624747f9844b8a5b3f92acf9a119705b1fbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:46:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] null patch: 59-own-worlds

Each bot has its own World: WorldName holds a hidden owner part, so Worlds keeps one World per bot and dimension, as a vanilla client has one level per connection. Every bot parses its own chunk packet (the section store shares equal sections). Other bots are ordinary entities in each bot's world. The shared-world code of patches 31 and 44 that cannot run any more is removed: the chunk-skip, the twin adoption, UpdatedBy and the per-client arbitration, and the bot-to-bot view (PeerView and its readers in pushes, picks, aim, entity clicks and placement). The patch 53 overlay stays.

Vanilla: ClientPacketListener#handleLogin / #handleRespawn (one ClientLevel per connection), #updateLevelChunk, #handleAddEntity, #handleMoveEntity. Grim: every check reads only the packets of its own bot (L4 contract tests).
